2026-08-16T15:34:02Z    [ADI:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: The proposed adjusted diluted EPS of $3.043/share is below ADI’s own FY2026 Q3 adjusted EPS guidance range of $3.15–$3.45 (midpoint $3.30 ± $0.15). A quarter EPS forecast that falls outside the company’s guided range, without a stated disconfirming update, is very likely wrong.
2026-08-16T15:34:36Z    [HD:Adjusted diluted EPS] GATE critic: Internal inconsistency: Using your stated inputs (FY2025Q2 adjusted diluted EPS = $4.68 and YoY growth = +0.05%), the calculation is 4.68 × 1.0005 = 4.68234, which rounds to 4.682 (3 dp) or 4.68 (2 dp). You instead cite 4.683 in the derivation and submit 4.68251, neither of which matches the stated math. Either the base figure or growth rate used differs from what you report, so the proposed $4.68251 is not reproducible from your described method.
2026-08-16T15:34:37Z    [ADI:Adjusted gross margin] GATE critic: The “last 4 reported levels” you averaged (69.9, 71.6, 74.1, 72.2) are not the last four Q3 adjusted gross margins. In your own cited table, these figures appear in mixed/duplicated columns (e.g., FY2020Q3 and FY2021Q3 lines are identical; FY2022Q3 and FY2023Q3 are identical), suggesting you pulled prior-year comparison values rather than the current-quarter figures and also omitted the most recent Q3s (FY2024Q3 and FY2025Q3). For a FY2026 Q3 seasonal average you should use the current adjusted GM for FY2022Q3–FY2025Q3; averaging 69.9/71.6/74.1/72.2 is a wrong-period/wrong-column basis.
2026-08-16T15:34:37Z    [DE:Diluted EPS (GAAP)] GATE critic: The aggregation rule is misapplied: you said a weighted median would be used under disagreement but claimed it’s undefined for two values and switched to a “weighted midpoint.” With the two candidates 4.39945 (weight 0.928) and 6.75971 (weight 0.072), the weighted median is defined and equals 4.39945 because the lower value’s cumulative weight exceeds 0.5. Using the midpoint inflated the result to 4.57048 USD/share instead of the correct robust aggregate implied by your stated approach.
