2026-08-16T15:34:52Z    [HAS:Net fees] GATE critic: You’re modeling a number that should already be reported. Your “post‑guidance signal” quotes explicitly reference H2 FY26 (“lower net fees in H2 26”), which implies FY2026 has closed and management has discussed it. By that point Hays will have disclosed the actual FY2026 Group net fees (GBPm) in its FY2026 results/annual report. Using a smoothed YoY decline from FY2025 and then a heuristic “signal tilt” is the wrong basis for a completed fiscal period; the published FY2026 net fees should be used instead.
2026-08-16T15:35:14Z    [DE:Production & Precision Ag operating profit] GATE critic: The aggregation step is methodologically wrong: you asserted that a weighted median is undefined for two values and defaulted to a weighted mean (yielding 471.128). For two candidates sorted by value, the weighted median is well-defined and equals the first value where cumulative weight exceeds 0.5. With 289.501 (weight 0.111) and 493.831 (weight 0.889), the weighted median is 493.831, not 471.128—so the submitted figure is based on an incorrect basis.
